{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_administration_finance_commit__000", "source": "Finance Committee «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Finance Committee «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Finance Committee «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nFinance Committee\nThe Finance Committee advises on the Institute’s budget, financial planning and resource allocation, and reports to the Governing Body.\nProf. B. N. Chaudhari\nChairperson\nShri. Suresh Mhatre\nExpert Nominee\nProf. Sudhir Dhage\nMember\nSK\nDr. Sujata Kulkarni\nDP\nDr. D. M. Patil\nDr. Deepak Karia\nDr. Anand Mane\nSmt. Pallavi More\nSmt. Sangita Fernandes", "filename": "spit_ac_in_administration_finance_committee.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/administration/finance-committee/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_administration_governing_body__000", "source": "Governing Body «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Governing Body «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Governing Body «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nGoverning Body\nThe Governing Body provides strategic direction and oversight to Bhavan’s Sardar Patel Institute of Technology, comprising management nominees, teaching members, an educationalist, an industrialist, and university and state government representatives.\nDr. Sesha Iyer\nChairman\nDr. Prachi Gharpure\nManagement Nominee\nDr. G. D. Yadav\nShri. Asif Mulla\nShri. Suresh Mhatre\nMember\nDr. Pooja Raundale\nTeaching Member\nProfessor, SPIT\nDr. Kiran Talele\nAssociate Professor, SPIT\nShri. Rahul Chari\nIndustrialist/Alumni Member\nCo-Founder & CPTO, PhonePe\nDr. Vikram Gadre\nMember (Educationalist)\nProfessor, IIT Bombay\nDr. B. N. Chaudhari\nPrincipal of the Institute\nDr. Pramod Naik\nState Govt. Nominee\nJoint Director, DTE\nProf. R. N. Awale\nUniversity of Mumbai Nominee\nProfessor, VJTI", "filename": "spit_ac_in_administration_governing_body.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/administration/governing-body/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__000", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nAdmissions 2026-27\nS.P.I.T. Highlights\nNumero Uno, Self-Financed, Empowered Autonomous Institution of Maharashtra.\n100 % Placement with Average Salary at par with IITs.\nConsistently ranked in the bracket of 100 to 150 by NIRF in the country.\nUnique, flexible, globally competent curriculum.\nStrong culture of innovation, research and entrepreneurship.\nConsistent winners of Industry organized technical competitions like Texas Instruments, ARM, KPMG & many more.\nFruitful industry association, Semester long industry internship.\nCET Percentile Comparison\nPrincipal's Letter\nNamaste, Dear Parents and Aspirants,\nI welcome you to Sardar Patel Institute of Technology – S.P.I.T.\nWe are Maharashtra’s numero uno self-financed, autonomous institute and a proud constituent of “Bharatiya Vidya Bhavan” – an 88 year movement built on values, by Dr. K.M. Munshi.\nParents, the question today is not just about a 4-year degree. It’s about the next 40 years of your child’s career. Career is not a 100-meter sprint, it is a marathon.\nThe world is changing very fast. AI, cloud computing, semiconductors, energy storage, quantum computing, fintech, cybersecurity – these are not just buzzwords anymore. This is the new language of India.\nA student graduating today will work for 50 years and change careers 3 to 4 times. What job roles will they have in their thirties and forties? Honestly, we don’t know. So, we asked ourselves: How do we prepare them?\nAt S.P.I.T., we prepare them for the WHY, and the HOW.\nHow do we do that? Three things:\nFirst: Learn by Doing, Not Just by Listening.\nWe have moved beyond conventional classrooms. We have introduced four “Studio Mode” core courses. This means that in core subjects, students don’t just sit in lectures. They build, prototype, code, and present – just like in a design studio or a startup. Learning by doing.\nSecond: Industry-Ready Minors.\nAlong with technical depth, we give breadth.", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__001", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Second: Industry-Ready Minors.", "text": "Second: Industry-Ready Minors.\nAlong with technical depth, we give breadth.\nA student can do a Minor in Management from SPJIMR or a Minor in Banking Technologies with Barclays – learn fintech, risk, digital banking directly from industry leaders.\nAlternatively, one can do a Minor in Computer or AIML while majoring in Electronics and Telecommunication.\nThere are several other minors to match every career path.\nWe even offer a Minor in specializations such as Mathematics / Physics / Systems Engineering.\nPlus: A Research Internship in 7th semester or an Industry Internship in 8th semester.\nEvery year around 50 of our students do a research internship at IITs/BARC/TIFR, and the remaining pursue the industry internship.\nStudents opting for the research internship continue their work in the eighth semester in the form of a project.\nSo, by the time you graduate, you already have 1 year of real research experience at elite institutions.\nThird: Values + Placements + Global Reach\nOur students are in Google, Microsoft, Intel, AMD, Facebook, Uber, JPMC, Barclays, Nvidia and several other deep tech companies.\nThey are in UCLA, San Diego, Columbia, ETH, Delft, Georgia Tech, Illinois, Stanford, Georgia Tech, CMU for MS programs.\nThey are winning national hackathons/ entrepreneurship challenges arranged by IITs/IIITs/IIMs/BITs/AICTE, and many international technical competitions.\nThey are doing it with empathy, with ethics, with the Bhavan culture.\nS.P.I.T. offers a “PI” model of Education; one compulsory minor with a chosen major, humanities, foreign languages, four studio projects, two minor projects, one major project, an opportunity to learn courses of interest from NPTEL platform.\n54% of the credits of the program are flexible leading to truly a choice-based credit system.\nThe UG curriculum is unique and aims at holistic development of the learners.", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__002", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Third: Values + Placements + Global Reach", "text": "54% of the credits of the program are flexible leading to truly a choice-based credit system.\nThe UG curriculum is unique and aims at holistic development of the learners.\nTo the Parents: 174 of the Fortune 500 companies have GCCs in India today. India’s Semiconductor, AI, Electronics, Quantum Missions are here. The jobs of tomorrow are here. S.P.I.T. is connected to the pulse of the nation. Our alumni have founded companies like PhonePe, WorkIndia, Dunzo, SKEWB, Thousand Eyes, Cash Flo, Symbol, Furnishka, and several others.\nTo the Students: these 4 years of engineering are not about marks and grades. They are about building things. Failing. Learning. Leading. We will facilitate you to articulate a great portfolio.\nAt S.P.I.T., we don’t just give degrees. We build technocrats who will lead in their chosen fields.\nSo, come, join us.\nLet’s learn together. Let’s build together. Let’s grow together.\nThank you\nProf. B. N. Chaudhari\nAdmission Programmes\nB.Tech.\nM.Tech.\nMCA\nPhD\nFor details regarding eligibility and admission procedure, please visit DTE / State CET Cell website, www.mahacet.org\nFor details regarding eligibility and admission procedure, please visit DTE / State CET Cell website, www.mahacet.org\nFor details regarding eligibility and admission procedure, please visit DTE / State CET Cell website, www.mahacet.org\nPh.D Electronics and Telecommunication\nPh.D Computer Engineering\nPh.D Electronics Engineering\nPh.D Master of Computer Applications\nFees\nFees approved by Fee Regulating Authority\nB.Tech: Rs. 2,12,000/- ( Fees are likely to be revised. The difference, if any, is to be paid by students as and when approved by the Fee Regulating Authority.)\nB.Tech - (Institute Level Fees): Rs. 4,26,125/-\nM.Tech: Rs. 1,00,000/-\nMCA: Rs. 1,47,000/-\nDSE: Rs. 2,10,000/-\nPlacements & Internships\nPlacements\n2025-26\n2024-25\n2023-24\n2022-23\n2021-22\n2020-21\n2019-20\nPlacements and Internships\nPercentage Placed\nInternships\nOur Recruiters\nCorporate Feedback", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__003", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Fees approved by Fee Regulating Authority", "text": "B.Tech - (Institute Level Fees): Rs. 4,26,125/-\nM.Tech: Rs. 1,00,000/-\nMCA: Rs. 1,47,000/-\nDSE: Rs. 2,10,000/-\nPlacements & Internships\nPlacements\n2025-26\n2024-25\n2023-24\n2022-23\n2021-22\n2020-21\n2019-20\nPlacements and Internships\nPercentage Placed\nInternships\nOur Recruiters\nCorporate Feedback\nWe take extreme pleasure in being associated with SPIT. Students from SPIT have been very analytical and creative in providing business solutions here at IVP. We anticipate your extended service for fulfilling our manpower requirements in a long run. – Indus Valley Partners\nOur organization has been associated with SPIT graduates for two years now and it has been a more than satisfactory experience.\nWe have been very impressed with the caliber of the candidates and we are quite keen to continue the relationship.\nThe Students are industry ready and well trained in technical skills.\nSoft Skills and Etiquette of the students is very good.\nTheir ability and adaptability to learn different technologies and skills, continuously improve and contribute to business has been very impressive.\nTheir value addition to the organization has been immense. – ISS | Institutional Shareholder Services\nThe students are technically sound and possess good logical skills. They are good at articulating their thoughts and ideas. – Quantiphi Analytics Solutions Pvt. Ltd.\nHigher Studies\nFew universities opted by students\nSP - Technology Business Incubator\nSupported by Dept. of Science & Tech. - Govt. of India\nRecently funded incubatees\nLiminal\nScholr\nRama Lifescience\nSkinzy\nZeuva\nAvileen Academic School Pvt. Ltd.\nRethynk Technologies Pvt. Ltd. (Eatabl)\nDVDP\nSome of our graduated startups:\nWork India\nQuiditch\nPykih\nVPS Tech\nEmbedos\nKan Innovation\nClick here to know more...\nLife @ SPIT\nOverview\nHighlights\nSports\nEntrepreneurship\nS.P.I.T. represents the true spirit of self-actualization, providing a perfectly balanced stage to nurture academic performance with personal growth.\nOur Alumni\nDistinguished Alumni\nRahul Chari, Co-Founder Phone Pe\nMohit Lad, CEO ThousandEyes\nDr. Nutan Limaye, Prof. IIT Bombay\nDr. Mayank Agarwal, Prof. IIT Patna\nNilesh Dungarwal, Co-Founder WorkIndia", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__004", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Our Alumni", "text": "Our Alumni\nDistinguished Alumni\nRahul Chari, Co-Founder Phone Pe\nMohit Lad, CEO ThousandEyes\nDr. Nutan Limaye, Prof. IIT Bombay\nDr. Mayank Agarwal, Prof. IIT Patna\nNilesh Dungarwal, Co-Founder WorkIndia\nDr. Ravi Todi, Qualcomm\nDr. Akshay Bhagwatwar, Program Manager, Amazon\nDr. Prashant Nair, Prof. University of British Columbia\nDr. Abhishek Sharma, Component Research Intel\nAlumni Speaks\nVikrant Potnis - Director Fortemagna Advisors\nDarshan Savalia - Co-Founder Skinzy Software\nKaran Shah - NVIDIA\nAunnasha Sengupta - Research Scholar @ University of Michigan\nNandish Avlani - Senior Design Engineer AMD\nJugal Gala - Product at Gartner, Stanford Engineering\nRuchir Kanakia - Co-Founder (Stealth Startup)\nPrutha Atre - Founder Indian Academy of Venture Capital\nTushar Ghadge - Lead Developer Fork Media Group\nTushar Ghadge - MCA\nResearch\nElectronics & Telecommunication Engineering\nAt a glance\nComputer Engineering\nComputer Science & Engineering\nProgram Overview\nThe Bachelor of Technology (B.Tech) in Computer Science and Engineering (CSE) at Sardar Patel\nInstitute of Technology (SPIT) is a comprehensive four-year undergraduate program designed to\nequip students with a solid foundation in computer science principles, engineering methodologies,\nand practical applications. The program emphasizes both theoretical knowledge and hands-on\nexperience to prepare graduates for the rapidly evolving field of technology.\nStudents are exposed to a curriculum that covers core areas such as mathematics, programming,\ndata structures, algorithms, computer networks, Computer Architecture and Organization ,\noperating systems, etc, while also delving into advanced topics like artificial intelligence, neural\nnetwork , soft computing, machine learning, data analytics, NLP, Image Processing, Signal Processing\n,Computer Vision, Explainable AI, Human Machine Interaction, cloud computing, Blockchain,\nQuantum computing and cyber security. Through a combination of classroom learning, laboratory\nwork, and real-world projects, the program ensures that students are not only proficient in technical\nskills but also adept at problem-solving and critical thinking.\nSPIT's B.Tech CSE program is designed to meet industry standards, with regular updates to the\ncurriculum to reflect the latest technological advancements. Graduates are well-prepared to pursue", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_admissions__005", "source": "Admissions 2026-27 «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Computer Science & Engineering", "text": "skills but also adept at problem-solving and critical thinking.\nSPIT's B.Tech CSE program is designed to meet industry standards, with regular updates to the\ncurriculum to reflect the latest technological advancements. Graduates are well-prepared to pursue\ncareers in diverse fields such as software development, Machine Learning, Data Visualization, Data\nscience, User Experience Design, Data Analysis, network security, Cloud computing, Backend and\nFront end development and more, or to continue their education with advanced degrees.\nThrough high-quality academic programs enriched with today's National Education Policy(NEP-2020)\nthat offer a unique blend of teaching, research, activity-based learning including Seva Satva, minors\netc. that strengthens learner’s ability to solve problems, expand knowledge base, work\nindependently, think critically, and find new ways to apply Science and Engineering concepts to\nbenefit society.\nIn addition to technical training, the program also focuses on the development of soft skills,\nteamwork, and leadership qualities, ensuring that students are well-rounded professionals ready to\ncontribute to the global tech industry.\nStudents work alongside faculty members who are leaders in their respective disciplines, have access\nto labs equipped with the latest technologies, and are connected to a comprehensive University\nproviding breadth and depth of opportunities. As a result, our students acquire critical thinking\ncapabilities as well as practically oriented skills that are prized by prestigious companies and\nacademic institutions of National and International Importance.\nAll faculty members of the Department of Computer Science and Engineering are strongly\ncommitted to supporting your success. In return, we know you will study hard, seek out and respect\nthe opinions of faculties and find opportunities to give back to your society. The efforts are\nconsciously planned for the overall development of students. This leads our students to become\ncompetent, innovative, socially-responsible and dynamic. We are confident that our students will\nemerge as assets not only to this institution but also to the entire society, and the nation at large.\nProgram Highlights, Core & Electives...\nMaster of Computer Application\nAdmissions Core Committee\nFirst Year Engineering Admissions Core Committee", "filename": "spit_ac_in_admissions.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/admissions/", "doc_type": "web"}
