{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_ariia__000", "source": "Atal Ranking of Institutions on Innovation Achievement (ARIIA) «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Atal Ranking of Institutions on Innovation Achievement (ARIIA) «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Atal Ranking of Institutions on Innovation Achievement (ARIIA) «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nAtal Ranking of Institutions on Innovation Achievement (ARIIA)\n2023\nARIIA 2023 Certificate\n2022\nARIIA 2022 Report\n2021\nARIIA 2021 Certificate [PDF]\nARIIA 2021 Report\n2020\nARIIA 2020 Certificate [PDF]\nARIIA 2020 Report\n2019\nARIIA 2019 Report\nARIIA 2019 Certificate", "filename": "spit_ac_in_ariia.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/ariia/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_best_practices__000", "source": "Best Practices «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Best Practices «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Best Practices «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nBest Practices\nSardar Patel Institute of Technology follows a set of best practices that go beyond conventional academics to support holistic student development and faculty growth. These practices reflect the institute’s commitment to learning, flexibility, mentorship, and empowerment, ensuring that students and faculty are supported at every stage of their academic and professional journey.\nResearch Internship\nSPIT actively encourages students to engage in research internships as a means of developing analytical thinking, problem-solving skills, and academic curiosity. These internships allow students to work on research-oriented problems under faculty guidance or at external institutions and laboratories, helping prepare them for higher studies, research careers, and innovation-driven roles.\nSupporting Documents / Links:\nResearch Internship Policy\nResearch Report 2024-25\nDeferred Placements\nSPIT has a formal deferred placement policy that allows students to delay immediate campus recruitment after graduation. This flexibility enables students to pursue entrepreneurship, freelancing, research, or focused skill-building for a defined period, while retaining the opportunity to return to campus placements in subsequent cycles if required.\nPlacement Policy\nPlacement Summary\nMentorship\nMentorship at SPIT follows a multi-layered approach involving faculty mentors, senior students, and alumni. Faculty provide academic and career guidance, while seniors and alumni share practical insights from their experiences, creating a supportive environment that fosters informed decision-making and personal growth.\nGeneral Mentorship Report 2024-25\nAlumni Mentoring\nNew Beginnings Mentoring\nStudent Empowerment Policy\nSPIT believes in empowering students by actively involving them in academic, technical, cultural, and administrative activities. Through leadership roles in committees, clubs, and institutional initiatives, students develop responsibility, confidence, and teamwork skills.\nStudents Empowerment Policy\nFaculty Empowerment Policy\nFaculty empowerment at SPIT focuses on academic autonomy, professional development, and leadership opportunities. Faculty members are encouraged to engage in research, training programs, curriculum development, and institutional governance, supporting continuous improvement and academic excellence.\nEmpowerment Policy for Faculty\nStudent Startup Policy", "filename": "spit_ac_in_best_practices.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/best-practices/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_best_practices__001", "source": "Best Practices «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Faculty Empowerment Policy", "text": "Faculty Empowerment Policy\nFaculty empowerment at SPIT focuses on academic autonomy, professional development, and leadership opportunities. Faculty members are encouraged to engage in research, training programs, curriculum development, and institutional governance, supporting continuous improvement and academic excellence.\nEmpowerment Policy for Faculty\nStudent Startup Policy\nStudent Startup Policy at SPIT, through SP-TBI, supports student-led ventures by providing access to incubation, mentorship, labs, workspace, and startup resources. The programme allows student founders to develop their ideas into real startups within a supportive entrepreneurial ecosystem, encouraging innovation, risk-taking, and long-term career growth.\nSP-TBI Student Startup Programme", "filename": "spit_ac_in_best_practices.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/best-practices/", "doc_type": "web"}
