{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_scholarships_vidya_lakshmi_po__000", "source": "Vidya Lakshmi Portal «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "Vidya Lakshmi Portal «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "Vidya Lakshmi Portal «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nVidya Lakshmi Portal\nNational Securities Depository Limited (NSDSL) e-Governance Infrastructure Ltd., has developed Vidya Lakshmi Portal. This portal has facilities of education loan, scholarship and other student friendly facilities through one link. The portal is gateway to Banks for education loan & also has linkages with National e-Scholarship Portal (NeSP).\n40 banks have been registered so far and 71 loan schemes have been uploaded in Vidya Lakshmi Portal.\nLink to: Vidya Lakshmi Portal", "filename": "spit_ac_in_scholarships_vidya_lakshmi_portal.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/scholarships/vidya-lakshmi-portal/", "doc_type": "web"}
{"chunk_id": "spit_ac_in_sp_it_teaching_learning_and_e__000", "source": "SP-IT Teaching, Learning, and Evaluation (TLE) Model: «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "page_or_section": "SP-IT Teaching, Learning, and Evaluation (TLE) Model: «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology", "text": "SP-IT Teaching, Learning, and Evaluation (TLE) Model: «  Sardar Patel Institute of Technology\nSP-IT Teaching, Learning, and Evaluation (TLE) Model:\nOutcome-Based Education System Overview\nSession 1:\nThis session introduces SP-IT, the concept of academic autonomy, and the philosophy of Outcome-Based Education (OBE) from both student and faculty perspectives. It covers SP-IT’s vision, mission, and foundational elements of OBE, such as:\nGraduate Attributes\nLearning Objectives (BL1-6)\nProgram Educational Objectives (PEO1-4)\nCourse Outcomes (CO1-6)\nProgram Specific Outcomes (PSO1-2)\nProgram Outcomes (PO1-12)\nWatch the full session here:Session 1\nSession 2:\nThis session defines OBE as a student-centered teaching methodology. In an OBE framework, course delivery and assessment are aligned to ensure students meet specific objectives and outcomes, emphasizing the measurement of student performance across various levels.\nWatch the full session here:Session 2\nSession 3:\nThis session provides guidance on creating an OBE course file. It explores different assessment methods, attainment targets, and compares outcomes within a closed-loop process for continuous improvement.\nWatch the full session here:Session 3\nSession 4:\nThis session is dedicated to establishing target levels for Course Outcomes (COs) and Program Outcomes (POs). It delves into strategies for scaling these outcomes using direct and indirect assessment methods, while also discussing the associated scaling factors. Additionally, the session highlights various publicly available resources from SP-IT designed to enhance teaching and learning for both students and faculty.\nWatch the full session here:Session 4\n1-CS_Cover_Page_Course_File\n2-Theory_Course_File_Index\n3-Lab_Course_File_Index\n4-CE203_CO attainment_Course_File\n5-CE203_Revised CAO_2024_25_syllabus\n6-CE_Vision Mission\n7-CS_Vision Mission\n8-EXTC_Vision Mission", "filename": "spit_ac_in_sp_it_teaching_learning_and_evaluation_tle_model.txt", "url": "https://www.spit.ac.in/sp-it-teaching-learning-and-evaluation-tle-model/", "doc_type": "web"}
